What:		/proc/<pid>/im_flag
What:		/proc/<pid>/task/<tid>/im_flag
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only 9R-compatible task identity bitmask followed by its
		human-readable tags.  The kernel refreshes the mask when a task's
		comm changes, avoiding repeated string comparisons in scheduler
		consumers.  This is separate from sched_assist's userspace-assigned
		ux_im_flag field.

What:		/proc/tpp_task_report
What:		/proc/tpp_tagged_list
What:		/proc/tpp_cpu_select_report
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only reports for the donor Task Placement Policy used by Unity
		worker threads.  The policy itself remains donor-default-off through
		/sys/module/tpp/parameters/tpp_on.  Enabling it first validates the
		msmnile three-cluster cpufreq topology; failure leaves it disabled.
		Optional large monitor buffers are allocated only when
		tpp_task_record_on is enabled.

Users:		OnePlus Android 14 game and performance services
